      "edition": "Wednesday 21 October",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Selection watch",
          "heading": "Seb Atkinson and Arthur Clark make England case in Gloucester's Bordeaux display",
          "body": "Gloucester's Seb Atkinson and Arthur Clark both pushed their England claims in round one of the Champions Cup, with Clark making a statement against Bordeaux-Bègles. Atkinson kept injecting himself into Gloucester's attack with his playmaking and carrying, while Clark posted eight tackles, seven carries, a try and an assist as the Cherry and Whites could have taken the win. That display should leave Steve Borthwick brimming, though the wider European round left him with questions."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "All Blacks beat Wallabies 43-21",
          "body": "Steve Tandy names 39-man Wales squad."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
