      }
    },
    "388": {
      "date": "2026-10-21",
      "edition": "Wednesday 21 October",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Contract news",
          "heading": "Alex Nankivell commits to Munster until 2029 with Ireland ambitions intact",
          "body": "Alex Nankivell has signed a two-year extension tying the New Zealander to Munster until 2029, and the centre's international ambitions are firmly in view. The 29-year-old joined from the Chiefs in 2023, has played 58 times for the province and was named Munster's 2026 Men's Player of the Year. He will be 32 when he completes World Rugby's residency rules in 2028. Munster general manager Ian Costello says the province hopes to see him \"realise that potential in the near future.\""
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "All Blacks beat Wallabies 43-21",
          "body": "Steve Tandy names 39-man Wales squad."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
