      }
    },
    "391": {
      "date": "2026-10-21",
      "edition": "Wednesday 21 October",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Selection call",
          "heading": "Tandy leaves out Macs Page despite four tries in four Scarlets appearances",
          "body": "Scarlets centre Macs Page is among the most eye-catching omissions from Steve Tandy's 39-man squad, despite four tries in four appearances this season. Scarlets director of rugby Nigel Davies said of the 21-year-old: \"He's probably the first name on the team sheet.\" Davies added: \"Steve will definitely be considering him.\" RUCK reports Page has received an offer from Munster, with no update since, and WalesOnline says he is likely to be the next cab off the rank if injuries strike."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "All Blacks beat Wallabies 43-21",
          "body": ""
        }
      ]
    },
    "460": {
      "date": "2026-10-21",
      "edition": "Wednesday 21 October",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Host bid",
          "heading": "Argentina lead four-nation South American bid to host 2035 Rugby World Cup",
          "body": "Argentina are leading a joint South American bid to host the 2035 Rugby World Cup, with Uruguay, Chile and Brazil joining them in the submission. Planet Rugby frames the proposal as a direct challenge to World Rugby's desire for a European return, making Argentina's case a test of how far the sport's governing body will look beyond Europe. World Rugby has yet to select the host, so the bid stays live until that decision lands."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "All Blacks beat Wallabies 43-21",
          "body": "Steve Tandy names 39-man Wales squad."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "RTÉ Sport Rugby"
      },
      "rung": "storyline"
    },
    "461": {
      "date": "2026-10-21",
      "edition": "Wednesday 21 October",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Bledisloe fallout",
          "heading": "Harry Wilson admits 'so much pressure' from All Blacks in Bledisloe losses",
          "body": "Wallabies captain Harry Wilson said after Saturday's second Bledisloe Test, a 43-21 loss in Sydney, that he 'probably never felt under so much pressure as in the last two games' against the All Blacks. Wilson and Fraser McReight are confident of doing well on the Nations Championship tour, which opens against England at Twickenham and also takes in Scotland and Wales. McReight said the Wallabies would have taken an undefeated Bledisloe series going in, and called the All Blacks 'world-class for a reason'."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Steve Tandy names 39-man Wales squad",
          "body": ""
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "Planet Rugby"
      }
    },
    "463": {
      "date": "2026-10-21",
      "edition": "Wednesday 21 October",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Eligibility rules",
          "heading": "Japan Rugby League One softens proposed rules restricting foreign-born players with Japanese passports",
          "body": "On 28 August, Japan Rugby League One backed down on proposed registration rules that would have restricted players holding Japanese passports but born abroad. Players who gained Japanese nationality before the end of May 2025 will now be treated the same as Japanese-born players when the 2026-27 season opens in December. Among the players who sued was Timothy Lafaele, who starred for Japan at the 2019 World Cup. The climbdown follows a backlash from players and fans, a league executive admitting it had underestimated the reaction."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "All Blacks beat Wallabies 43-21",
          "body": "Steve Tandy names 39-man Wales squad."
        }
      ]
    },
    "465": {
      "date": "2026-10-21",
      "edition": "Wednesday 21 October",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Team gesture",
          "heading": "All Blacks go out early to acknowledge Nathan Charles before Sydney Test",
          "body": "On Saturday in Sydney, the All Blacks left the dressing room a couple of minutes early so they could go and see Nathan Charles on the field. The former Wallabies hooker, 37, recently revealed his Motor Neurone Disease diagnosis, and the whole team went over to him, shook his hand and hugged him before the All Blacks' 43-21 win. Both teams united in support of Charles, and captain Codie Taylor presented him with a framed All Blacks jersey signed by the squad."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Steve Tandy names 39-man Wales squad",
          "body": ""
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "Planet Rugby"
      }
    },
    "467": {
      "date": "2026-10-21",
      "edition": "Wednesday 21 October",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Squad boost",
          "heading": "Warren Whiteley confirms Springboks have joined Sharks ahead of Cardiff clash",
          "body": "Several Springboks have joined the Sharks ahead of Friday's URC clash against Cardiff at the Arms Park, forwards coach Warren Whiteley confirmed on Tuesday. Captain André Esterhuizen, Edwill van der Merwe, Ethan Hooker, Ox Nché and Thomas du Toit were rested for last Saturday's 40-33 away win against Lyon, and Whiteley said the group has had only one session together. He knows of no injury concerns, adding that they are all available and all flew across."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "All Blacks beat Wallabies 43-21",
          "body": "Steve Tandy names 39-man Wales squad."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "SA Rugby Magazine"
      }
    }
